To integrate HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for a solar system simulation, you need to ensure that your HTML provides a canvas for drawing, your CSS styles the page and canvas appropriately, and your JavaScript handles the logic for rendering and animating the planets. Below, I'll provide an overview of how to do this, along with tips for optimizing performance and enhancing the visual appeal of your simulation.

### HTML (index.html)

The HTML file should contain a `<canvas>` element where the solar system will be rendered. It also includes links to the CSS and JavaScript files.

```html
